  "equipment_type": "Make-up air unit controller",
  "applies_to": "Greenheck make-up air units with the factory microprocessor controller, MUA program v4.1.",
  "summary": "Greenheck's make-up air controller (program v4.1) offers BACnet MS/TP, BACnet IP, Modbus RTU and Modbus TCP. The BMS can enable the unit, command occupancy, reset alarms, write occupied and unoccupied temperature setpoints, supply limits, lockouts, static pressure and damper setpoints, take over the supply fan and outdoor air damper and send sensor values while a watchdog is kept alive. Read-only objects cover temperatures, outputs, unit status mode, latest alarm and bit-packed status and alarm words.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP",
    "BACnet IP"
  ],
  "firmware": "MUA v4.1",
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "Appendix E prints a Modbus register beside each BACnet object; only the BACnet side is listed here.",
    "Status and alarm words are bit-packed (IV objects with AV copies); the bit tables are in the manual.",
    "Source: Appendix E Points List, manual pages 36-40 (118 objects)."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "Microprocessor Controller for Make-up Air - Reference Guide (MUA v4.1)",
    "doc_number": "487036",
