  "integration": {
    "summary": "With BACnet licensed and the protocol set in Network Settings, enable the unit with BV 2, command occupancy with BV 3, write the occupied temperature setpoint AV 1 and reset alarms with BV 4. Keep the BV 1 watchdog toggling if the BMS sends sensor values or controls the fan or damper. Monitor Unit_Status_Mode (AV 41), supply temperature, Global_Alarm (BV 19) and LatestAlm.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "BV 2",
        "name": "System_Enable",
        "why": "Enables or disables the unit"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 3",
        "name": "BMS_Occupancy_Command",
        "why": "Occupancy; Active = Unoccupied, Inactive = Occupied"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 1",
        "name": "Temperature_Setpoint",
        "why": "Occupied temperature setpoint"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 1",
        "name": "BMS_Watchdog",
        "why": "Heartbeat when BMS controls fans or sensors"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 4",
        "name": "Reset_All_Alarms",
        "why": "Remote alarm reset"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 41",
        "name": "Unit_Status_Mode",
        "why": "Current operating mode code"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 2",
        "name": "Supply_Temp_Analog_Input",
        "why": "Supply (discharge) air temperature"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 19",
        "name": "Global_Alarm",
        "why": "Alarm output (any or shutdown alarms)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "IV 9",
        "name": "LatestAlm",
        "why": "Most recent alarm code"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "BV 2 System_Enable enables or disables the unit; BV 3 BMS_Occupancy_Command sets occupancy (Active = Unoccupied).",
    "heartbeat": "BV 1 BMS_Watchdog must be toggled by the BMS within the timeout delay (15 minutes by default, adjustable) whenever the BMS replaces a hardwired sensor (or takes over fan speed or damper control). If the timer expires, the controller alarms (BMS Offline) and falls back to its hardwired sensors and local control until the BMS returns. The watchdog status is shown on a read-only BV.",
    "remote_sensors": "Set the source-select BV to BMS (BV 6 outside temp, BV 9/10 CO2, BV 12 space static, BV 13 space temp), then write the matching *_from_BMS value (AV 30, 33, 34, 36, 37). BV 14 and BV 15 hand supply fan speed and damper position to the BMS. The watchdog must be kept alive.",
    "setup": [
      "BMS protocol (BACnet MS/TP, BACnet IP, Modbus RTU or Modbus TCP) and its settings are in the Network Settings menu; the service password 1000 is needed to change them.",
      "After changing BACnet MS/TP or IP settings, enable 'Save Settings' and reboot the controller (cycle power or hold the main menu button 3 seconds).",
      "BACnet must be licensed on the controller; alarm 20 'BACnet License Not Installed' means it is not."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "Status and alarm words (IV and paired AV objects) are bit-packed; decode them with the bit tables in the manual.",
      "Remote sensor values are only used while their source-select BV is set to BMS and the watchdog is alive.",
      "Alarm 54 'BMS Frequent Writes' means the BMS writes too often; reduce the write rate."
    ]
  }
